PolicyManagerClearSetupTest
├── When no setup was ever committed
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoSetup carrying the caller and the action.
├── When the setup was already cleared
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoSetup carrying the caller and the action.
├── When the setup was already cleared and the named nonce is wrong
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoSetup rather than a wrong nonce.
├── When the named nonce is not the current one
│   ├── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongSetupNonce carrying the named nonce and the current one.
│   └── It should change nothing.
├── When the named nonce is from before a recommit
│   ├── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongSetupNonce carrying the earlier nonce and the current one.
│   └── It should leave the later setup in place.
├── When a setup exists
│   ├── It should zero the commitment and move the nonce by exactly one.
│   ├── It should write the current block as setupCommittedAtBlock.
│   ├── It should leave the next attempt id where it was.
│   ├── It should emit SetupCleared alone with the new nonce.
│   └── It should reach no other contract.
├── When an attempt is waiting
│   ├── It should set the attempt to Cancelled and keep the rest of its record.
│   ├── It should emit AttemptCancelled with a zero canceller before SetupCleared.
│   ├── It should leave the attempt counter where it was.
│   └── It should reach no method and no pause read.
├── When the action stopped serving the account
│   ├── It should zero the commitment and move the nonce by exactly one.
│   ├── It should cancel the waiting attempt.
│   └── It should not ask the action.
├── When the stored nonce is the largest uint64
│   └── It should revert with the arithmetic overflow panic and change nothing.
├── When the block number is the largest uint48
│   ├── It should zero the commitment and move the nonce by exactly one.
│   └── It should store the largest uint48 as setupCommittedAtBlock.
├── When the block number is past the width of the block field
│   ├── It should revert with SafeCastOverflowedUintDowncast carrying the width and the block number.
│   └── It should change nothing.
├── When the last attempt is no longer waiting
│   └── It should emit SetupCleared alone and leave the record untouched.
└── When an address other than the account calls
    ├── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoSetup carrying that address and the action.
    └── It should leave the account's setup and waiting attempt untouched.
